  "conclusion": "The Duprat velocity scale removes almost all false separation on both the flat-plate centre and SUBOFF, so the published pressure-gradient scaling is structurally superior to a u_tau-only Van-Driest closure. It is not yet an admissible force model: on the validated flat-plate centre its shear is 7.94% below the production Musker baseline, while on SUBOFF its attached-only shear is 25.59% above the frozen production wall law. No coefficient was selected using the SUBOFF experiment. Both ODE variants remain diagnostic until an independent adverse-gradient canonical benchmark and reverse-shear closure pass."
